From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: dcp: drive the HDMI port of a T8132
 dcpext

The HDMI port of the J604 (M4 MacBook Pro 14-inch) hangs off a T8132
external display coprocessor: ATC2 as a four-lane DisplayPort PHY, the ATC2
display crossbar and an on-board DP-to-HDMI converter, with the hot-plug,
converter power and port power GPIOs of the M1/M2 and M3 Pro HDMI ports
(t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi on dcpext0).

An adopted T8132 dcpext returns from probe before the generic fixed output
code, which needs a non-M4 IOMFB, so nothing took that output. Take it after
the adoption, as that code does (DP PHY, HPD GPIO and its interrupt, converter
and port power, crossbar output, PHY DisplayPort mode), inside a devres group:
the session is pinned by then, so an output that cannot be taken is left out
with a warning and the Type-C routes go on. Its suppliers are waited for before
the adoption, as the routes' are.

The output connects through the existing fabric code (dcp_fabric_run_hdmi(),
dcp_hdmi_connect_fixed()), with the hybrid behaviour of the M3 Pro: a Type-C
display may borrow the pipeline, and its release restores the HDMI route
while HDMI is plugged. The firmware can connect it only once the adopted
IOMFB session is open and the DPTX remote port service is published, which
come after probe: a start work enables the HPD interrupt and acts on the
level then. It is kicked by probe (after the Type-C routes, which the HDMI
presence logic counts), the DPTX publication, the IOMFB session start and
resume, with bounded retries for a missed kick; the decision is a pure fabric
core function with a KUnit case (S50g). System sleep and remove stop it.

The DRM connector of a dcpext described with an HDMI-A connector is HDMI-A,
and the converter service requests of dcp-hdmi.c are forwarded for the T8132
too (a firmware that refuses them ends the polling).

[j604: Not run on the
 J604 yet: the HDMI connect, the converter requests on T8132 firmware and the
 PHY state after system sleep are to be verified at the desk
 (HDMI check).]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit aa9c3cecd03b9138bc504d3ca58c024830d46a46)
